Lena (Docs): Drafted a short migration note for the invoke/tool-calling changes and pushed a tiny PR: https://git.company/infra/docs/pulls/512
Ravi (SDK): Thx — are we replacing `generate()` with `invoke()` everywhere in the examples or only in v2 snippets?
Lena (Docs): Only v2 examples. I added a compatibility block that shows the old call and the new one side-by-side.
Tessa (Eng-ML): Please include a canonical tool response shape for lists where items can be null. Customers hit that with scraping results.
Lena (Docs): Added this schema in the PR: 

```
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "results": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": { "anyOf": [ { "type": "object" }, { "type": "null" } ] }
    }
  },
  "required": ["results"]
}
```

Ravi (SDK): Nice. Can we also show a parsing example that tolerates trailing commas and falls back to a sanitized parse? Both sync and streaming variants would help.
Lena (Docs): Will add both. Streaming pattern I'll include is minimal: 

```
let buffer = ''
for await (const chunk of client.stream(res)) {
  buffer += chunk
  try { return JSON.parse(buffer) } catch (e) { /* wait for more */ }
}
return fallbackParse(buffer)
```

Marco (Product): Add a short release-note blurb that points to the migration guide and call out the SDK rename. Also mark old snippets with a deprecation banner.
Kai (SRE): If you add example validation, I can wire a tiny GH action to run a `docs-examples-validate` job so malformed JSON blocks fail CI.
Lena (Docs): Perfect — can you open the action PR? We can merge that first so this examples PR is safer to land.
doc-bot: preview created: https://deploys.company/docs/preview/2350012345
Erin (Support): I'll scan the checklist for on-prem customers and note any extra steps around older SDK binaries.
Tessa (Eng-ML): One more: add a short note about empty arrays vs null when a tool intentionally returns no results. Helps parsing expectations.
Lena (Docs): Added that note and an example fallback snippet. Tagging reviewers now. Thanks all :pray:
